"Facets are seeds that grow only in the soil of what a skill has already established."
"They give a skill new facets without altering its fundamental nature."
"An original skill can offer hundreds of facets; some need others first, some are locked for now."
"Divide From Whole helps a bearer divide a burden from its source; many facets require it."
"Sensitivity lets the bearer sense the qualities of the thing being divided from the whole."
"Bearer facets can take on memory, disease, sound, pain or stress, and darker burdens."
"A bearer feels everything preserved in some way, so pain-bearing facets hurt the bearer."
"Burden of Enchantment lifts enchantments off objects and preserves them, leaving them mundane."
"Burden of Spell holds unattached spells, some castable later, some harmful when released."
"Burden of Wordchain takes on others' wordchain debt."
"Burden of Secret takes a spoken secret out of the entruster's mind while it is preserved."
